Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8. Mylar Independent Spectral Validation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dfb76398-5d0e-384c-abca-6d477453f90f"],

Cell["\<\
This section provides an independent spectral validation of the correction \
and forward model established with polystyrene. The required inputs are the \
Mylar FTIR spectrum and the measured Mylar QCL spectrum already expressed on \
the frozen polystyrene-corrected wavenumber axis, together with the \
independently specified QCL linewidth, selected Mylar reference-peak centers, \
and common Gaussian fitting half-window. Mylar thickness and absorption \
coefficient support the separate absolute-absorbance relation but are not \
consumed by mylarRun; refractive index and incidence angle enter the \
interference analysis in Section 9, and the number of averages remains \
acquisition metadata. Any literature-derived Mylar optical constants are \
attributed to [CITATION NEEDED]. The FTIR spectrum is convolved in \
transmission space at the measured QCL setpoints and compared with the QCL \
measurement through residuals, root-mean-square error, mean and maximum \
residuals, correlation, paired Gaussian peak centers and widths, and an \
overlay of the reference, measured, and predicted spectra. Agreement \
therefore tests transfer of the calibration and spectral-response model to a \
material that did not determine either model. The notebook neither refits the \
polystyrene correction to Mylar nor applies a calibration transformation \
within mylarRun, preserving the distinction between calibration and \
validation and preventing the independent specimen from optimizing the \
prediction.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"646e3d72-5b1e-a34e-84cf-f0dea247dc6e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

