Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10. HRP\[Dash]CO States, Bands, and Initial Population", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7b22047f-2519-4545-95e8-cb302af6e3e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This section establishes the HRP\[Dash]CO state scheme, parameter set, \
spectral forward prediction, and dark-state conformer populations used in the \
subsequent photolysis and rebinding analyses. In ferrous HRP\[Dash]CO, CO is \
directly coordinated to the heme iron,",
 StyleBox["2",
  FontVariations -> {"Superscript" -> True}],
 " and the complex exhibits pH-dependent bound-CO bands near 1905 and 1934 \
cm^-1.",
 StyleBox["3,4",
  FontVariations -> {"Superscript" -> True}],
 " The two bands have been reported to recover with indistinguishable rate \
constants under the studied pH 6 conditions, supporting their treatment with \
a shared kinetic model.",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontVariations -> {"Superscript" -> True}],
 " The experimental 532 nm pump setting closely matches the 530 nm excitation \
used in the cited HRP flash-photolysis study.",
 StyleBox["5",
  FontVariations -> {"Superscript" -> True}],
 " Required inputs comprise the sample temperature and pH or pD; HRP and \
dissolved-CO concentrations; optical path length; measured FTIR and QCL \
spectra; QCL linewidth and fit window; fitted band widths; peak molar \
absorptivities and relative integrated strengths; and the independently \
determined photochemical, spatial-overlap, kinetic, repetition-rate, and \
recovery-criterion parameters used in later sections. A constrained \
simultaneous two-Gaussian fit with a linear baseline yields the band centers, \
full widths at half maximum, integrated areas, and strength-corrected \
conformer fractions, while the FTIR-to-QCL forward model yields the predicted \
QCL spectrum, residual spectrum, agreement metrics, and spectral overlay. \
These results establish the population weighting used to predict the bound-CO \
bleach and test whether the measured QCL spectrum is consistent with the FTIR \
reference. The conformer fractions are inferred from measured band areas \
rather than imposed; fitted centers, widths, and populations remain results \
of the fit and are not written automatically into the reader-editable \
parameter association, and their interpretation retains the reported \
temperature, pH or pD, units, and uncertainty in the relative integrated \
strengths."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9959884948851585`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"bb7ce438-b2a2-b840-9e7c-\
27bed38e721c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hrpStateTable", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "\n", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<State\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Physical assignment\>\"", ",",
          " ", "\"\<Expected IR marker\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Role in model\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<HRP(FeII)-CO conformer 1\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Bound CO conformer\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<1905 cm^-1 literature center\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Dark-state population f1905\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<HRP(FeII)-CO conformer 2\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Bound CO conformer\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<1934 cm^-1 literature center\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Dark-state population f1934\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<P\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Photodissociated CO in or near distal pocket\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Bound-CO bleach; pocket CO marker not assumed\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Geminate rebinding or escape\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Ferrous HRP plus CO in solvent\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Bound-CO bleach\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Slow CO-dependent rebinding\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Recovered HRP(FeII)-CO\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Re-established dark conformer equilibrium\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Recovery of both bound-CO bands\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Final state\>\""}], "}"}]}], "\n", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Alignment", " ", "->", " ", "Left"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Background", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Lighter", "[", 
           RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "0.90"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "None"}], 
         "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", "hrpStateTable"}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9959884950826473`*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[67]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d9225de7-9e5b-ab4b-bc48-5539e39e0d30"],

