Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["11. HRP\[Dash]CO Pump Photons and Initial Photolyzed Fraction", \
"Section",ExpressionUUID->"19606b71-435d-a04e-8260-498b4a84e54a"],

Cell["\<\
This section quantifies the HRP\[Dash]CO pump-photon budget and the initial \
photolyzed fraction within the probe-sampled volume. Required inputs are the \
pulse energy at the sample, pump wavelength, base-10 pump absorbance, \
photolysis quantum yield, pump\[Dash]probe overlap fraction, effective \
overlap area, HRP concentration, and optical path length. The incident photon \
number is determined from E\[Lambda]/(hc), the absorbed photon number is \
obtained by applying the spatial-overlap factor and the absorbed fraction 1 \
\[Minus] 10^\[Minus]A, and the number of illuminated HRP molecules is \
calculated from concentration, overlap volume, and the Avogadro constant. \
Multiplication by the quantum yield and normalization by the illuminated \
molecule count gives the predicted initial photolyzed fraction, which is \
capped at unity. The displayed calculation reports incident and absorbed \
photons in the overlap volume, illuminated molecules, and the initial \
photolyzed fraction. Separate average- and peak-fluence helper relations are \
defined but are not evaluated by this result. The photon budget defines the \
initial condition for the kinetic and difference-absorbance models and \
establishes whether the expected signal is compatible with the delivered pump \
energy. Its interpretation assumes that incomplete spatial overlap is \
represented adequately and remains conditional on the absence of unmodeled \
saturation, multiphoton excitation, local heating, beam-profile \
nonuniformity, or spatial variation in the photolyzed fraction.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"41baaedb-93c7-734a-a09a-8d862da937a2"],

