Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14. Mb\[Dash]CO States, Bands, and Initial Population", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3f0a8caf-8276-e34a-8d3d-93813857b8e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This section establishes the Mb\[Dash]CO state scheme, parameter set, \
spectral forward prediction, and dark-state conformer populations used by the \
subsequent photolysis and kinetic analyses. The literature starting centers \
for the bound A0, A1, and A3 substates are approximately 1966, 1945, and 1933 \
cm^-1, respectively,",
 StyleBox["6",
  FontVariations -> {"Superscript" -> True}],
 " while photodissociated CO at the primary docking site gives B1 and B2 \
markers near 2131 and 2119 cm^-1.",
 StyleBox["6,7",
  FontVariations -> {"Superscript" -> True}],
 " The 532 nm pump wavelength is supported by its established use in \
nanosecond Mb\[Dash]CO flash photolysis.",
 StyleBox["8",
  FontVariations -> {"Superscript" -> True}],
 " Required inputs comprise sample temperature and pH or pD; Mb and \
dissolved-CO concentrations; optical path length; measured FTIR and QCL \
spectra; QCL linewidth and fit window; fitted band widths; peak molar \
absorptivities and relative integrated strengths; and the independently \
determined photochemical, overlap, kinetic, repetition-rate, and \
recovery-criterion quantities used in later sections. A constrained \
simultaneous three-Gaussian fit with a linear baseline yields the A-state \
centers, full widths at half maximum, integrated areas, and \
strength-corrected populations, while the FTIR-to-QCL model yields the \
predicted QCL spectrum, residuals, agreement metrics, and overlay. These \
results define the conformer-weighted bound-band bleach and test spectral \
consistency between the two instruments. Because the B1 and B2 markers lie \
above the installed 1638.8\[Dash]2077.3 cm^-1 QCL range, they identify \
inaccessible states rather than measured positive bands. The literature \
centers remain fit starting values, the actual sample populations are \
determined from measured FTIR areas rather than assumed, and fitted centers, \
widths, and populations are not written automatically into the \
reader-editable parameter association."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9959884949018555`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"2a57ebc6-065a-4b40-b310-\
221d269e3993"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mbStateTable", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "\n", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
