Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["15. Mb\[Dash]CO Pump Photons and Expected Difference Absorbance", \
"Section",ExpressionUUID->"860703cb-0e01-f141-ae99-489dd0fbc40f"],

Cell["\<\
This section converts the Mb\[Dash]CO pump exposure into an initial \
photolyzed fraction and defines the corresponding light-minus-dark difference \
absorbance within the installed QCL range. The displayed photon-budget \
calculation requires the pump pulse energy and wavelength, base-10 pump \
absorbance, photolysis quantum yield, pump\[Dash]probe overlap fraction and \
area, Mb concentration, and path length. It determines the incident and \
absorbed photon counts, illuminated-molecule count, and photolyzed fraction \
with the same photon-balance and overlap-volume relations used for \
HRP\[Dash]CO, and the fraction is capped at unity. A separately defined \
difference-spectrum function additionally uses the fitted A-state populations \
and their band centers, widths, and peak molar absorptivities to construct \
the conformer-weighted bound-state absorptivity. When that function is \
invoked, the initial difference spectrum is the photolyzed fraction \
multiplied by concentration and path length and by the difference between \
photolyzed- and bound-state absorptivity. Under the implemented assumption of \
zero photoproduct absorption at the probed bound-CO wavenumbers, the result \
is a negative conformer-weighted bleach. The displayed association therefore \
establishes the photon budget and initial population, while the separate \
spectral relation supplies signal shape, sign, and amplitude. Interpretation \
retains the light-minus-dark sign convention and the same overlap, \
saturation, heating, and spatial-uniformity considerations as the HRP \
calculation; verified photoproduct absorption within the installed range \
would invalidate the zero-photoproduct-absorptivity approximation at that \
wavenumber.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8c4f6c33-e832-ea4e-8bb6-b9f6901beed0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"DeltaA", "[", 
  RowBox[{"nu", ",", " ", "0"}], "]", " ", "==", " ", "f0", "*", 
  "concentration", "*", "pathLength", "*", "(", 
  RowBox[{
  "epsilonPhotolyzed", "[", "nu", "]", " ", "-", " ", "epsilonBound", "[", 
   "nu", "]"}], ")"}]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"5923bb93-ef7b-3844-b5e2-cb8fb8dd996a"],

