Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["19. Lock-In Filter Settling and Scan-Dwell Distortion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"91488f6a-e663-1440-b451-1da6a9248d1f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This section quantifies whether each stepped QCL measurement allowed the \
HF2LI demodulator to approach its steady-state response and estimates the \
spectral distortion associated with incomplete settling. The experimentally \
determined inputs comprise low-pass order, per-stage time constant, total QCL \
dwell time, QCL tuning delay, target settled fraction, and recorded \
sinc-filter state; an ideal spectrum and Gaussian peak center and window are \
additional arguments for the scan-distortion functions. The HF2LI response is \
represented by n cascaded first-order stages, and the order-dependent 3 dB \
and noise-equivalent power bandwidth factors follow the HF2 User Manual.",
 StyleBox["10",
  FontVariations -> {"Superscript" -> True}],
 " The available stable-measurement interval is the nonnegative difference \
between dwell and tuning times. The analytic step response yields settled \
fraction, settling error, target settling time, and both bandwidths, while an \
exact matrix-exponential state update propagates the cascade through \
successive spectral points. When the scan-distortion function is evaluated, \
Gaussian fits to the ideal and simulated ascending and descending spectra \
yield centers, widths, directional shifts, and hysteresis. These quantities \
establish whether the selected dwell preserves peak position and linewidth. \
The scan simulation initializes the first point at steady state, and no \
scan-distortion result is evaluated automatically in this section. The \
recorded sinc-filter state is not included in the propagation, so results \
with that filter enabled do not describe the complete HF2LI response."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
