Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["20. Temporal Instrument Response", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f4f897ba-aef4-7e45-80b6-f51918c05641"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This section estimates how finite optical and electronic response times \
transform an underlying pump\[Dash]probe transient. The inputs comprise a \
true transient function, simulation increment and limits, measured pump-pulse \
FWHM, probe-gate width, RMS timing jitter, installed detector-amplifier time \
constant, and HF2LI time constant and filter order. The detector-series \
documentation reports model-dependent time constants, so the entered \
detector-plus-amplifier value corresponds to the exact installed \
configuration or its direct measurement rather than a series-wide surrogate.",
 StyleBox["11",
  FontVariations -> {"Superscript" -> True}],
 " Pump FWHM is converted to Gaussian standard deviation and combined in \
quadrature with jitter; normalized discrete Gaussian and odd-length \
rectangular kernels represent optical timing and probe gating, and causal \
first-order updates represent the detector and lock-in stages. The defined \
transient-response function produces true and predicted measured traces and \
their overlay when supplied with a transient function. A separate \
impulse-response function begins with a unit-area discrete impulse and \
reports the response trace, sampled FWHM, area, and plot; the response is not \
explicitly renormalized after finite-window convolution, so the reported area \
reveals truncation. These results define the temporal resolution against \
which kinetic features are judged. Numerical accuracy depends on an increment \
that resolves the narrowest kernel, a window that begins in the pre-event \
baseline or steady state and contains the response, and sufficient padding to \
avoid edge artifacts. The model represents linear time-invariant blurring \
rather than saturation or other nonlinear detector behavior."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9959884949217205`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"5a66bd6d-3d89-9c4f-9e9a-\
df5d0721dddf"],

