Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["23. Measured SNR, Noise-Equivalent Absorbance, and Averaging", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6740f566-26d5-e74f-959c-224f6f0cf38e"],

Cell["\<\
This section derives noise and signal-to-noise metrics directly from \
fixed-wavenumber absorbance records and transient baselines. The inputs \
comprise the time\[Dash]absorbance baseline trace, the defined transient \
signal amplitude and pre-pump baseline standard deviation, the lock-in \
noise-equivalent bandwidth, the single-acquisition standard deviation and \
number of independent averages, and the sampling interval and cluster sizes \
used for the stability analysis. The baseline mean, standard deviation, \
peak-to-peak excursion, and duration are calculated from the trace; transient \
SNR is the absolute signal amplitude divided by baseline standard deviation, \
noise-equivalent absorbance is the same standard deviation divided by the \
square root of bandwidth, and ideal averaging follows the N^\[Minus]1/2 \
relation. Nonoverlapping cluster means additionally yield Allan deviation as \
a function of averaging time. These outputs test the detector/electronics \
prediction, quantify usable sensitivity, and reveal the averaging interval \
beyond which drift limits further improvement. Interpretation assumes that \
the selected baseline represents the same stationary, pre-pump acquisition \
condition; the averaging law applies only to statistically independent \
samples, and each Allan-deviation point requires at least two complete \
clusters.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ef236ffc-7ea3-c342-864f-0d792e66f101"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"baselineStatistics", "[", "baselineData_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"<|", "\n", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<MeanAbsorbance\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
       RowBox[{"baselineData", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<SDAbsorbance\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", 
       RowBox[{"baselineData", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<PeakToPeakAbsorbance\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
        RowBox[{"baselineData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
        RowBox[{"baselineData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Duration_s\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
        RowBox[{"baselineData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
        RowBox[{"baselineData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "\n", 
    "|>"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"transientSNR", "[", 
    RowBox[{"signalAmplitude_", ",", " ", "baselineSD_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "signalAmplitude", "]"}], "/", "baselineSD"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"noiseEquivalentAbsorbance", "[", 
    RowBox[{"baselineSD_", ",", " ", "equivalentBandwidthHz_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"baselineSD", "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "equivalentBandwidthHz", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"averagingPrediction", "[", 
    RowBox[{"sigmaSingle_", ",", " ", "independentAverages_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"sigmaSingle", "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "independentAverages", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"allanDeviation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "data_", ",", " ", "sampleInterval_", ",", " ", "clusterSizes_List"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"m", ",", " ", "clusterMeans"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", "cluster"}], ";", "\n", 
        RowBox[{"clusterMeans", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Mean", " ", "/@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"data", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "m", ",",
             " ", "m", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"m", "*", "sampleInterval"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"If", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", "clusterMeans", "]"}], " ", ">", " ", 
             "1"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Differences", "[", "clusterMeans", "]"}], "^", "2"}],
                "]"}], "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "\"\<InsufficientClusters\>\"", "]"}]}], 
           "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "\n", "]"}], ",", "\n", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"cluster", ",", " ", "clusterSizes"}], "}"}]}], "\n", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9959884952796364`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[164]:=",ExpressionUUID->"62d0675c-3527-3b46-94d9-c0564b8c33ab"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["24. Monte Carlo Uncertainty Propagation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"401ab213-6f8b-4249-8d58-159c1bf8fb3f"],

Cell["\<\
This section propagates experimentally determined input uncertainties through \
the coupled absorbance, photolysis, spectral-resolution, temporal-resolution, \
and noise calculations. The inputs are probability distributions for path \
length, concentration, peak molar absorptivity, pump energy and wavelength, \
pump absorbance, photolysis quantum yield, spatial overlap and overlap area, \
true peak center, intrinsic Gaussian spectral standard deviation, QCL \
linewidth and step, calibration offset, timing jitter, pump and probe widths, \
detector and lock-in time constants, lock-in order, and absorbance noise, \
together with the number of draws. Each draw produces Beer\[Dash]Lambert \
absorbance and photolyzed fraction, quadrature spectral and \
Gaussian-equivalent temporal widths, a calibration-shifted peak position, \
dark absorbance, initial transient-amplitude magnitude, and the sampled \
absorbance-noise value. Median, 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles, mean, and \
standard deviation summarize each output, retaining nonlinear transformations \
and asymmetric intervals. The sampler does not impose physical bounds; they \
are retained only when encoded in the supplied distributions. Association \
entries are sampled independently, lock-in-order draws are rounded, and \
correlated inputs require a joint-sampling construction. The temporal width \
is an approximation distinct from the full convolution in Section 20, the \
absorbance-noise entry is propagated rather than derived, and the absence of \
a fixed random seed permits finite-sample variation between evaluations.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"646a7d47-bad1-4041-8aaa-663c1b53e17e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

