Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["26. Required Outputs for the Supplemental Information", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8477d27f-5be2-854f-bb2e-37779249baa2"],

Cell["\<\
This section defines the publication-facing outputs assembled from the \
completed calculations and fitted data. The inputs are the finalized \
parameter and uncertainty tables, calibration and validation spectra, fitted \
HRP\[Dash]CO and Mb\[Dash]CO results, lock-in distortion simulations, \
temporal-response traces, dual-detector and Allan-deviation analyses, and the \
predicted-versus-measured comparison table. No additional numerical \
transformation is performed here; the upstream results are organized as Table \
S1, Figures S1\[Dash]S9, and Table S2 so that the experimental inputs, model \
validation, kinetic fits, instrument-response effects, noise behavior, and \
residual comparisons are presented as a coherent supplemental record. This \
output set establishes traceability from each reported claim to its inputs \
and calculation. The assembled tables and figures correspond to fully \
assigned inputs and visually inspected fits, and their captions, units, \
uncertainty definitions, and data provenance remain consistent with the \
values represented in the notebook.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f50ef6f3-a2d0-544f-b8cc-425ad88f4600"],

Cell["\<\
Table S1: all experimental inputs, uncertainties, units, and sources.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e0296ecf-5419-9e45-a00b-6430f54fa800"],

Cell["\<\
Figure S1: polystyrene FTIR, measured QCL, forward-predicted QCL, and \
residual.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a38356a7-11c5-1441-866c-4e81406cc2c3"],

Cell["\<\
Figure S2: calibration residuals versus wavenumber, elapsed time, and scan \
direction.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6763d6cc-b162-464d-aa75-09edb0a66e39"],

Cell["\<\
Figure S3: Mylar independent-validation overlay and residual.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"93bc077a-92fa-ef44-bd2b-74c053777a26"],

Cell["\<\
Figure S4: HRP\[Dash]CO two-conformer FTIR fit and recovered population \
fractions.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8e4251b4-c6f6-e048-8a7e-7e8b206b4b44"],

Cell["\<\
Figure S5: HRP\[Dash]CO measured transient with pocket/solvent model and \
residual.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a6e7681c-11ee-764d-b3e8-965560ec9ca3"],

Cell["\<\
Figure S6: Mb\[Dash]CO conformer fit, single-exponential fit, two-branch fit, \
and residual comparison.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6a66e9e5-4290-cc4e-8c0c-28b1a31675f0"],

Cell["\<\
Figure S7: measured and predicted lock-in scan-direction distortion.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f8a415b2-9cee-dd41-a8d0-c59e83e76e4c"],

Cell["\<\
Figure S8: true versus instrument-blurred transient and instrument-response \
function.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4b34322e-3b8f-9e41-a0e2-10fdc261c1f9"],

Cell["\<\
Figure S9: dual-detector noise before and after normalization, including \
Allan deviation.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b48cccf8-211a-5c48-969c-a4ef7f48a6a0"],

Cell["\<\
Table S2: predicted values, 95% intervals, measured values, and residuals.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"995437fa-2f28-1a4a-bae3-5285ecf6572b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["27. References and Data Provenance", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"120b21bd-dce5-4547-992d-94d4a2f3ab0c"],

Cell["\<\
This section records the bibliographic basis for the literature parameters, \
state assignments, and manufacturer specifications used throughout the \
notebook. Its inputs are the verified primary-literature and exact \
installed-device sources; no scientific quantity is calculated. The section \
outputs the numbered RSI-style reference list, which complements the source \
fields in parameter tables and the dataset provenance maintained with the \
corresponding repository records. This separation distinguishes literature \
starting values and state assignments from measurements and fits obtained for \
the present instrument and samples, supporting reproducibility without \
implying that a literature value was measured here. Manufacturer \
specifications apply only to the identified hardware variant and stated \
conditions, and any unverified mapping remains marked [CITATION NEEDED] \
rather than inferred.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a19126b5-4465-4c47-b190-d103bc79e7a6"],

